 1. System Objective: 

The primary objective of the Supply Chain & Warehouse Logistics Network Management System is to provide a centralized, robust relational database platform to track inventory across multiple geographically distributed warehouses, manage supplier purchasing workflows, monitor multi-stage shipment logistics, and support multi-level component assembly operations. 

Specifically, the system addresses key operational capabilities:

-Multi-Warehouse Inventory Visibility: Tracking real-time stock levels of products across different physical locations. 
-Automated Restock Threshold Tracking: Monitoring stock levels against predefined minimum reorder thresholds to trigger inventory replenishment. 
-Bill of Materials (BOM) Management: Supporting recursive structures where complex products are assembled from sub-components. 
-End-to-End Logistics Tracking: Managing supplier purchase orders and tracking shipments between source and destination warehouses. 

2. User Requirements vs. System Capabilities (ISO 29148):

A. User Requirements (UR)

-UR-01 (Warehouse Manager): The Warehouse Manager must be able to view inventory balances across all physical warehouses and record stock movements. 
-UR-02 (Procurement Specialist): The Procurement Specialist must be able to create purchase orders for suppliers when product stock falls below minimum thresholds. 
-UR-03 (Logistics Coordinator): The Logistics Coordinator must be able to dispatch shipments between warehouses and update arrival statuses. 
-UR-04 (Assembly/Production Supervisor): The Assembly Supervisor must be able to inspect product structures to identify sub-components required for assembling higher-level finished goods. 

B. System Capabilities (SC)

-SC-01 (Data-Centric Inventory Control): The system shall maintain an accurate quantity_on_hand for every product-warehouse pair. 
-SC-02 (Automated Restock Alerting): The system shall evaluate stock balances against min_reorder_level and raise alerts when stock is depleted. 
-SC-03 (Recursive BOM Traversal): The system shall support recursive relationships allowing arbitrary depths of component-subcomponent relationships. 
-SC-04 (Audit & Status Tracking): The system shall track status updates (Pending, Completed, Canceled, In-Transit) for purchase orders and shipments. 
